msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:49
msgid "2. Upload the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:51
msgid "Open the ``08-Bluetooth_lcd.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\bluetooth\\08-Bluetooth_lcd``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:55
msgid "The sketch needs the **LiquidCrystal I2C** library. Open the Library Manager, search for ``LiquidCrystal I2C`` and install it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:58
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:60
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. You should read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:68
msgid "If you read ``[!] no reply from the module``, the module is not answering on D0/D1 - check the four wires and the power supply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:73
msgid "3. Send Text with LightBlue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:75
msgid "Use the same **LightBlue** app as in the Get Started chapter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:77
msgid "Open LightBlue, tap **Scan** and connect to **SunFounder-C2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:79
msgid "Expand the service **0xA002** and open the characteristic **C304**. Then tap **Write new value**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:84
msgid "Set the format in the top right corner to **UTF-8 String** and type a short word - for example ``hello``. The picture shows the field just before sending:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:90
msgid "Send it. The word appears on the **LCD** and in the Serial Monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:94
msgid "Keep the text short: the LCD has 16 columns and 2 rows, and everything after the first 16 characters moves to the second row. A longer word is simply cut off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:97
msgid "To send text the other way - from the board to the phone - subscribe to **C305** and then type in the Serial Monitor. This is the same pair of characteristics you used in the Get Started chapter, only one side now drives an LCD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:103
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:105
msgid "**The LCD on the I2C bus**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:112
msgid "``0x27`` is the I2C address of the display, ``16`` is the number of columns and ``2`` the number of rows. Most of these modules answer on ``0x27``; a few use ``0x3F``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:115
msgid "**Bluetooth in one line**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:122
msgid "``BLEStream`` hides all the AT commands. ``bleSerial.begin()`` switches Bluetooth on, sets the name **SunFounder-C2** and starts advertising; after that the object behaves like an ordinary serial port - ``available()``, ``read()``, ``write()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:128
msgid "The module talks to the board over D0/D1 (``Serial1``) at **115200**. That is a hardware port, so no bit is lost even while the LCD is being updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:131
msgid "**setup()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:145
msgid "``lcd.backlight()`` matters: without it the display works but stays dark. The short ``setTimeout(50)`` stops ``readString()`` from waiting a full second for more characters that will never come."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:149
msgid "**loop() - phone to LCD**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:163
msgid "The phone often adds a line ending to what you type. Only those characters are removed - never a real character - and then the text is written to the display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:166
msgid "**loop() - board to phone**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/08-iot_Bluetooth_lcd.rst:174
msgid "Anything you type in the Serial Monitor is forwarded to **C305**. Subscribe to it in LightBlue and the characters appear there, byte by byte."
msgstr ""
